While parked it averages the GNSS fix and reports an honest error (the scatter of correlated
GNSS errors shrinks with the *effective* number of samples, not the raw count). It tags every
Wi-Fi scan and BLE sighting with that position and feeds the RV desktop's BeaconFix over its LAN
API. Everything that cannot be delivered is queued in SQLite and flushed on reconnect.
See docs/AGENT.md for the maths, the protocol and troubleshooting.
"""
